Hi everyone,
I’m currently learning AI integrations and could really use your help with a problem I’ve run into.

I’ve built a custom AI RAG assistant workflow using Flowise. I log every user question and answer to Google Sheets using a Make.com webhook via post-processing in Flowise.

The issue is this:
I can't get both proper answer formatting in the widget and accurate, consistent logging to Google Sheets to work at the same time.

Here's what happens:
- If I log the variable Answer (i.e., rawOutput) in the webhook payload, the formatting is preserved, but some answers differ from what is actually shown to the user in the widget.
- If I log the variable answer (modified inside the post-processing script), the logged answer matches what the model says in the widget, but the formatting breaks completely (extra quotes, backslashes, flattened text, etc.).
- 
I tried declaring **_let answer = Answer_** to preserve formatting while keeping things in sync — but as soon as I do that, the formatting breaks again.

So I’m stuck: either I get clean formatting OR consistent logging, but not both.

I know I’m missing something obvious, but I can’t figure it out.

Would really appreciate any help, suggestions, or workarounds!

Thanks in advance 🙏
